WEBVTT

00:21.521 --> 00:22.397
What the hell?

00:25.275 --> 00:26.359
Who the fuck are you?

00:35.869 --> 00:38.496
Come on, you son of a bitch.

00:38.997 --> 00:39.998
You bastard!

00:43.460 --> 00:44.461
Fuck.

00:45.628 --> 00:46.463
Let's go.

00:52.761 --> 00:54.471
Woo-jin. Let's call an ambulance.

00:54.554 --> 00:57.015
Gun-woo, things could get serious.

00:57.098 --> 00:58.808
A man is dying.

01:15.867 --> 01:16.826
Hyeon-ju.

01:16.910 --> 01:18.995
An old homeless man was injured badly,

01:19.079 --> 01:21.164
so we called an ambulance.

01:21.247 --> 01:22.624
What about Yang Jae-myeong?

01:23.541 --> 01:24.459
He ran away.

01:24.542 --> 01:26.503
Fuck! I told you not to interfere!

01:26.586 --> 01:28.379
But he was badly hurt.

01:28.463 --> 01:29.756
We had no choice.

01:29.839 --> 01:32.008
You don't even know him.
Why did you interfere?

01:32.092 --> 01:34.010
Yes, but--

01:39.307 --> 01:40.141
What do we do?

01:45.438 --> 01:46.397
I'll give her a call.

01:53.404 --> 01:56.282
- What?
- Hyeon-ju. About this…

01:56.783 --> 01:58.201
We are really sorry.

01:58.284 --> 02:00.161
This was 100% our fault.

02:00.245 --> 02:03.039
Where are you?
I want to go apologize in person.

02:03.123 --> 02:05.375
Forget it. It's over.

02:05.458 --> 02:08.128
Hyeon-ju, just give us
five minutes of your time, please?

02:08.628 --> 02:11.047
I am not kidding around at all.

02:11.131 --> 02:14.008
I'm really sorry about this.
Gun-woo also wants to apologize.

02:14.509 --> 02:16.761
Please, give us five minutes.

02:17.345 --> 02:18.179
Please.

02:18.680 --> 02:20.348
Come to the bookstore.

02:32.235 --> 02:33.444
Woo-jin.

02:35.488 --> 02:37.323
To be honest, I don't get it.

02:37.407 --> 02:38.616
What? Get what?

02:39.200 --> 02:42.745
If we had done nothing,
that homeless old man could've died.

02:42.829 --> 02:43.746
You saw it yourself.

02:44.330 --> 02:45.165
I did.

02:45.248 --> 02:48.293
We did the right thing,
so why do you have to apologize like that?

02:48.376 --> 02:52.213
- Why do we have to apologize?
- This was our first time on the job.

02:52.714 --> 02:55.341
Hyeon-ju wasn't here,
so it's hard for her to understand.

02:56.551 --> 02:59.137
We still don't know each other well,
and this happened.

02:59.220 --> 03:02.307
If we apologize for things
that might cause misunderstandings,

03:02.807 --> 03:04.642
I think we'll be able to communicate.

03:06.603 --> 03:08.605
- But…
- Gun-woo.

03:08.688 --> 03:11.733
I don't think you did anything wrong.

03:11.816 --> 03:13.484
But for the sake of the job,

03:14.360 --> 03:17.655
we should be able to smooth this out
if we help each other a bit.

03:18.406 --> 03:20.325
Just this once, okay?

03:22.368 --> 03:24.162
Yes, okay.

03:48.937 --> 03:52.315
BLOODHOUNDS

04:00.323 --> 04:02.700
Don't sit. This will be quick.

04:03.534 --> 04:05.161
Did you fight Yang Jae-myeong?

04:05.787 --> 04:07.872
It was unavoidable.

04:07.956 --> 04:09.624
We can't work together.

04:12.168 --> 04:13.169
What?

04:13.253 --> 04:14.796
Isn't it obvious?

04:15.380 --> 04:16.881
We gave you a sincere apology.

04:16.965 --> 04:19.217
I don't need an apology!

04:20.385 --> 04:23.179
Yang Jae-myeong saw your faces, didn't he?

04:24.097 --> 04:27.350
My plan was to tail him
and gather evidence quietly.

04:27.433 --> 04:30.561
Now that Yang Jae-myeong knows
someone is on his tail, he'll lie low.

04:30.645 --> 04:33.398
Therefore, my plan is ruined.

04:33.481 --> 04:35.858
We wore caps and masks.
He couldn't have seen our faces.

04:35.942 --> 04:39.487
Right. Since you covered your face,
there's no way he'd recognize you.

04:39.570 --> 04:42.156
Since this shitty hair was covered,
he wouldn't recognize you!

04:42.240 --> 04:44.617
Fuck! I'd recognize you from a mile away!

04:45.743 --> 04:47.870
What are you doing? Get out.

04:47.954 --> 04:50.081
- We apologized.
- I said get out!

04:50.164 --> 04:51.708
- We had no choice.
- How so?

04:51.791 --> 04:53.251
It's our first time working together.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.086
- We're not perfect!
- That's why I refused you!

04:55.169 --> 04:56.212
We acted accordingly!

04:56.296 --> 04:57.797
- According to what?
- I told you earlier!

04:57.880 --> 04:59.090
You don't fucking get it!

04:59.173 --> 05:00.842
Why did you bring up my hair?

05:00.925 --> 05:02.093
- We'll leave.
- Fuck.

05:02.176 --> 05:03.845
So stop screaming, please.

05:05.096 --> 05:06.931
I'll find a way to return

05:08.391 --> 05:10.727
the money Mr. Choi gave me.

05:12.770 --> 05:17.358
Since Woo-jin and I listened
to your yelling,

05:18.443 --> 05:19.986
please listen to me too.

05:26.367 --> 05:29.203
If someone offered
to make your work go smoothly

05:30.621 --> 05:32.332
in exchange for killing someone,

05:33.416 --> 05:34.500
could you do it?

05:47.764 --> 05:50.266
The Smile Capital boss
cut my face with a knife.

05:51.309 --> 05:54.395
If I had done nothing
while a man was dying in front of me,

05:55.188 --> 05:57.523
I'd be worse than that guy.

05:59.317 --> 06:00.735
It would be wrong.

06:03.404 --> 06:04.697
Think about it.

06:40.149 --> 06:43.111
I'll find some other place.
Don't worry too much.

06:44.487 --> 06:46.739
I'm sorry. I couldn't hold back.

06:47.532 --> 06:49.492
You held back better than I did.

06:50.868 --> 06:53.704
Are you hungry? Let's go
to this hangover soup place I know.

06:55.581 --> 06:56.749
Wait a second.

06:58.209 --> 07:00.628
It's probably closed
because of COVID. It's past ten.

07:03.005 --> 07:05.216
That just made me more hungry.

07:05.800 --> 07:06.926
I forgot.

07:10.221 --> 07:11.305
My stomach hurts.

07:12.890 --> 07:15.226
It's not my fault they're closed
because of COVID.

07:16.144 --> 07:18.062
It's your fault for bringing it up.

07:19.439 --> 07:22.316
You couldn't hold yourself back
with Hyeon-ju just now!

07:22.400 --> 07:24.235
You said that I did a good job.

07:24.318 --> 07:26.654
I said that
because you were moping like a loser.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.448
I wasn't moping like a loser.

07:29.907 --> 07:32.785
"I wasn't moping like a loser."

07:33.619 --> 07:34.912
What are you doing?

07:34.996 --> 07:37.999
I'm imitating you, you loser.
"Man, I'm hungry."

07:38.082 --> 07:40.084
- "My stomach hurts."
- Wow.

07:40.585 --> 07:42.086
You're so ugly.

07:44.338 --> 07:45.882
How could you joke like that?

07:45.965 --> 07:48.509
What? I wasn't joking. I'm being serious.

07:49.594 --> 07:52.555
I'm seriously hurt by this, so apologize.

07:58.352 --> 08:01.272
SORRY, I WAS WRONG. SEE YOU AT THE OFFICE
TOMORROW AT 10:00 A.M.

08:02.231 --> 08:03.065
Woo-jin.

08:04.984 --> 08:08.362
I knew we'd get through to her!

08:51.322 --> 08:54.492
Hey, it's short!

08:54.575 --> 08:55.409
- Short.
- Short!

08:55.493 --> 08:57.453
You're so damn loud!

08:58.538 --> 09:00.373
Don't get mad. It's just a game.

09:00.456 --> 09:01.707
- That's expensive.
- Why so mad?

09:01.791 --> 09:04.126
- Hurry up and go.
- God, I will!

09:04.210 --> 09:05.044
It's your turn.

09:05.127 --> 09:07.588
YANG JAE-MYEONG
I'M WAITING IN FRONT OF THE GOLF SHOP

09:07.672 --> 09:09.799
- You have to wear your mask, sir.
- Got it.

09:14.053 --> 09:15.096
What is it?

09:16.097 --> 09:18.057
Someone is tailing us, sir.

09:19.725 --> 09:20.601
Who was it?

09:21.352 --> 09:23.896
They were young,
but they knew how to fight.

09:24.897 --> 09:25.731
Are you sure?

09:26.315 --> 09:28.818
- What?
- Are you sure someone's tailing you?

09:30.611 --> 09:31.487
Focus.

09:31.571 --> 09:32.572
The thing is…

09:33.781 --> 09:34.615
Talk.

09:34.699 --> 09:36.659
Before I started working for you,

09:36.742 --> 09:38.828
I borrowed some money from a place.

09:38.911 --> 09:41.289
They didn't mention wanting it back,
so I ignored the fuckers.

09:41.372 --> 09:42.248
Get to the point.

09:42.331 --> 09:44.166
But they came for the money recently.

09:44.250 --> 09:47.128
The bastard that came to collect
was wearing a hat with a red cat on it.

09:47.628 --> 09:50.840
The punk who got the jump on us today
was wearing the same hat.

09:53.926 --> 09:55.011
Not a coincidence?

09:56.762 --> 09:58.306
No. It was the same cap, sir.

10:02.810 --> 10:04.228
Where did you borrow the money?

10:04.312 --> 10:06.814
To explain yesterday's situation briefly,

10:06.897 --> 10:09.275
Yang Jae-myeong had already robbed
that homeless man,

10:09.358 --> 10:11.736
but he had forgotten about that.

10:11.819 --> 10:14.363
So it resulted in a fight
when he started a conversation.

10:16.157 --> 10:18.034
But how much money

10:18.117 --> 10:20.870
do Jae-myeong's guys borrow
with one stolen ID?

10:21.912 --> 10:23.706
About 50 million won per mule account.

10:24.373 --> 10:26.167
That's 500 million for ten stolen IDs.

10:26.250 --> 10:28.419
Jeez. How long have they been doing this?

10:29.754 --> 10:31.756
At least for half a year, I think.

10:31.839 --> 10:35.051
Wow! They must have made quite a fortune.

10:36.135 --> 10:39.180
Did those loan sharks
just sit back and do nothing?

10:39.263 --> 10:41.724
They'll be investigated by the cops
if they report it.

10:41.807 --> 10:45.019
They're trying to recover the money
on their own but aren't able to.

10:47.188 --> 10:48.522
This is my plan.

10:48.606 --> 10:51.192
Find the private loan sharks
that Yang Jae-myeong conned

10:51.275 --> 10:54.070
and recover the money
Yang Jae-myeong stole for a commission.

10:55.488 --> 10:58.157
With a 1% commission,
that's three billion won.

10:58.908 --> 10:59.950
We should charge 2%.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.208
Woo-jin.

11:08.459 --> 11:10.336
If loan sharks get conned,

11:10.419 --> 11:13.631
wouldn't that make things worse
for the people who got loans from them?

11:14.215 --> 11:15.341
What?

11:15.424 --> 11:18.427
They'd have to harass their clients more
to recoup their losses.

11:19.011 --> 11:19.887
So?

11:20.429 --> 11:24.392
I just thought small businesses
would suffer the most.

11:25.559 --> 11:26.977
You're right about that.

11:27.061 --> 11:27.895
Yes.

11:40.741 --> 11:42.076
How did they find us?

11:42.910 --> 11:44.370
How did they find us?

11:44.453 --> 11:45.287
I don't know.

11:48.541 --> 11:50.668
Turn off the lights and the sign outside.

11:50.751 --> 11:51.877
Damn it!

11:55.506 --> 11:57.758
PYEONGHWA BOOKS

11:59.093 --> 12:00.803
- Turn your phones off.
- Okay.

12:08.185 --> 12:09.437
Is it here? Are you sure?

12:09.520 --> 12:10.438
Yes. I'm sure, sir.

12:18.571 --> 12:20.698
You borrowed money from a bookstore?

12:21.323 --> 12:24.577
Yes. The owner used to be
a big moneylender back in the day.

12:41.886 --> 12:43.929
Hey, give this a kick.

12:54.064 --> 12:54.940
Kick here.

12:57.276 --> 12:58.944
Hurry up, you bastard.

13:06.118 --> 13:07.870
- Kick harder.
- What?

13:07.953 --> 13:09.580
Kick harder, you bastard!

13:09.663 --> 13:10.706
Damn it.

13:12.458 --> 13:13.292
Harder!

13:14.376 --> 13:15.211
Harder!

13:15.711 --> 13:17.296
Kick harder, you bastard!

13:21.759 --> 13:22.593
That's enough.

13:23.928 --> 13:26.180
We'll need heavy equipment
to tear this down.

13:29.016 --> 13:30.351
This here is the safe.

14:10.140 --> 14:13.894
Last night on your way back,
did you check if you were being tailed?

14:15.062 --> 14:17.314
Well, we took the bus.

14:17.898 --> 14:19.984
They could have followed the bus.

14:20.901 --> 14:24.947
If they had tailed us last night,
why didn't they jump us right away?

14:25.030 --> 14:26.615
Why make their move now?

14:27.199 --> 14:30.077
- He might've wanted to bring Kim Jun-min--
- Hyeon-ju.

14:30.160 --> 14:32.371
Yang Jae-myeong saw
how we fought last night.

14:32.454 --> 14:35.124
If he wanted to jump us,
he would've brought more people.

14:36.083 --> 14:38.919
They probably weren't sure either.

14:39.003 --> 14:42.506
But they might have caught on now.

14:46.760 --> 14:50.472
Anyway, it's important to find out
how those people found us.

14:50.556 --> 14:53.017
That's how we'll prevent
making the same mistake twice.

14:53.100 --> 14:54.643
Okay. I totally understand.

14:54.727 --> 14:58.230
Why don't we sit down for a chat? Yes?

15:06.238 --> 15:08.365
Does Yang Jae-myeong know of this place?

15:09.074 --> 15:10.492
He came here a long time ago.

15:11.911 --> 15:16.081
That means he's caught onto
our connection with this place somehow.

15:16.582 --> 15:17.958
Right.

15:20.544 --> 15:21.545
Yes.

15:25.883 --> 15:26.759
Well…

15:27.927 --> 15:30.137
He could've recognized your cap, right?

15:31.597 --> 15:33.766
The thing is,

15:33.849 --> 15:37.603
I followed you a while back
when you were chasing down a homeless man.

15:37.686 --> 15:38.771
Oh…

15:40.105 --> 15:42.524
Yes, that was me.

15:43.025 --> 15:45.778
The homeless man back then
was Yang Jae-myeong.

15:46.362 --> 15:47.863
I see. Crap.

15:47.947 --> 15:51.408
I was wearing
that cap back then, wasn't I?

15:51.992 --> 15:54.745
Yes. Your hat left quite the impression.

15:56.288 --> 15:58.499
Then that might've been
how they found out.

15:58.582 --> 16:01.961
But why do you think
they kicked the shutters?

16:02.544 --> 16:05.923
Our shutters were custom-made
with steel, not aluminum.

16:06.006 --> 16:07.341
They were checking for that.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.843
Damn, I think they'll be back.

16:12.221 --> 16:13.263
Why is he here?

16:30.489 --> 16:31.949
What were you guys doing?

16:33.117 --> 16:35.077
That white car came here, didn't it?

16:37.037 --> 16:38.205
Speak up.

16:41.166 --> 16:43.752
I am sorry, sir. It's my fault.

16:44.586 --> 16:47.798
We went out on a job last night.

16:47.881 --> 16:49.049
What kind of job?

16:49.133 --> 16:51.176
The thing is…

16:53.637 --> 16:54.471
What kind of job?

16:56.557 --> 16:58.100
We were tailing Yang Jae-myeong.

16:59.018 --> 16:59.852
Why?

16:59.935 --> 17:02.855
Grandpa, loan sharks are desperate
to catch Yang Jae-myeong.

17:02.938 --> 17:05.399
I'm sure they'll be willing to pay for it.

17:05.899 --> 17:08.235
And I happen to be
the only one who can catch him.

17:09.236 --> 17:10.487
Is this about money?

17:10.571 --> 17:12.322
It's good to make money.

17:14.074 --> 17:15.451
What did you guys do?

17:16.452 --> 17:19.121
They are my bodyguards, aren't they?

17:20.748 --> 17:22.041
I'm not hurt.

17:22.833 --> 17:24.293
I'm disappointed in you.

17:26.253 --> 17:28.255
I'm disappointed in you too, Grandpa.

17:28.338 --> 17:30.466
It's clear Yang Jae-myeong is
up to no good.

17:30.549 --> 17:31.925
Why aren't you doing anything?

17:32.009 --> 17:35.471
Mr. Hwang could get rid of him
with a snap of his finger!

17:35.554 --> 17:38.640
Are you frustrated?
I'm even more frustrated!

17:39.850 --> 17:42.603
Gun-woo, take off that bandage.

17:42.686 --> 17:44.438
- What?
- Hurry up and do it.

17:45.355 --> 17:47.024
What? Okay.

17:50.736 --> 17:53.489
If Yang Jae-myeong and Kim Jun-min
keep conning loan sharks,

17:53.572 --> 17:56.200
they'll inevitably threaten
and tighten their grip

17:56.283 --> 17:58.702
on powerless people like Gun-woo.

17:58.786 --> 18:03.123
That would effectively render
all the charity work you do meaningless.

18:03.207 --> 18:06.085
Your money will go straight
into their pockets!

18:06.752 --> 18:09.338
If you really want to help those in need,

18:09.421 --> 18:12.549
you should weed out the punks
like Yang Jae-myeong first.

18:14.384 --> 18:16.095
Who did that to your face?

18:18.680 --> 18:20.557
The Smile Capital boss did it, sir.

18:22.101 --> 18:22.935
What's his name?

18:23.018 --> 18:26.188
Well, I don't know his name.

18:27.648 --> 18:30.400
He had a long knife scar
running down his left cheek.

18:39.076 --> 18:39.993
Go back home.

18:57.719 --> 18:58.554
Sir.

18:59.763 --> 19:01.598
Could it just be a coincidence?

19:02.099 --> 19:05.477
Please check if Kim Myeong-gil is
the CEO of Smile Capital.

19:05.978 --> 19:06.812
Yes, sir.

19:14.194 --> 19:16.238
Juju.

19:17.489 --> 19:18.365
What?

19:18.448 --> 19:20.617
You called us your bodyguards.

19:20.701 --> 19:23.287
I have to say, that felt good.

19:23.370 --> 19:24.371
So?

19:24.454 --> 19:27.916
So I thought it might be nice
to talk casually.

19:28.000 --> 19:30.002
We are a team, after all, Juju.

19:30.085 --> 19:32.629
So, we're not a team
if we don't speak casually?

19:32.713 --> 19:36.717
It's a suggestion because it'd be nice
if we could work as one big happy family.

19:37.217 --> 19:40.971
If we're a family, the oldest
should treat the rest to a meal.

19:41.054 --> 19:42.097
Are you buying?

19:42.723 --> 19:45.017
I prefer sticking
to the formalities, ma'am.

19:45.726 --> 19:46.768
I'm kidding.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.104
Let's use Grandpa's credit card.
What do you want?

19:49.188 --> 19:50.022
Rib eye.

19:50.731 --> 19:51.565
Then you pay.

19:53.442 --> 19:54.276
A barbecue buffet.

19:54.359 --> 19:57.446
- A barbecue buffet?
- Yes. I know a great place.

20:01.074 --> 20:02.576
Well, all right.

20:02.659 --> 20:03.493
Let's go!

20:06.747 --> 20:08.999
How long have you been friends
with Gun-woo?

20:09.917 --> 20:13.253
I don't think it matters
how long you've known a person.

20:13.337 --> 20:16.089
Knowing someone a long time
doesn't mean you're real friends.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.007
So?

20:17.090 --> 20:18.800
What really matters is

20:18.884 --> 20:21.762
how similar your life trajectories are.

20:21.845 --> 20:25.849
To be able to understand one another,
even after a short conversation.

20:25.933 --> 20:27.392
That's important.

20:27.476 --> 20:29.645
- And that's you two?
- Right.

20:29.728 --> 20:34.399
Besides, boxers like us exchange more than
just our fists in an exchange of blows.

20:34.983 --> 20:36.985
"So that's the kind of life you've lived."

20:37.069 --> 20:37.903
Pow!

20:37.986 --> 20:39.529
"This is how I've lived."

20:39.613 --> 20:42.783
Each blow contains

20:42.866 --> 20:47.913
the fighters' character,
heart, experience, hysteria…

20:49.248 --> 20:50.123
History?

20:50.749 --> 20:51.917
History.

20:53.210 --> 20:55.879
We see it all. We know it all.

20:56.755 --> 20:57.589
Sure.

20:58.173 --> 20:59.549
Besides, Gun-woo is

21:01.343 --> 21:03.053
a senior Marine.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.014
And that tells you everything.

21:06.682 --> 21:08.225
What exactly does it tell you?

21:09.893 --> 21:11.144
Everything.

21:11.228 --> 21:12.437
Everything about what?

21:12.521 --> 21:15.565
Juju, this isn't something
that can be explained.

21:15.649 --> 21:17.317
It's just a Marine thing.

21:17.401 --> 21:20.195
It's like when rappers use hip-hop
as an all-encompassing term

21:20.279 --> 21:23.657
when they look at something
and go, "This is hip-hop."

21:23.740 --> 21:25.284
It's indescribable.

21:25.367 --> 21:27.911
I see. Indescribable, you say?

21:28.704 --> 21:30.998
- Are you mocking me?
- Of course not.

21:31.081 --> 21:32.416
This stuff is really…

21:32.499 --> 21:33.625
- Here.
- Right.

21:37.838 --> 21:38.672
What?

21:39.923 --> 21:41.925
You haven't even turned on the grill yet?

21:42.009 --> 21:43.176
You never told me to.

21:43.260 --> 21:45.971
It's customary for whoever is
at the table to turn on the grill.

21:46.054 --> 21:48.348
I didn't know.
Why didn't you turn it on and go?

21:48.432 --> 21:51.518
How could I? The grill would've burned
by the time I came back.

21:51.601 --> 21:53.312
How would iron burn up?

21:53.395 --> 21:55.105
It's not the iron that burns.

21:55.188 --> 21:58.942
I'm saying that the meat will burn
if the grill is too hot.

21:59.026 --> 22:00.152
So the meat will burn.

22:00.235 --> 22:02.446
That's what "burning the grill" is.

22:02.529 --> 22:05.949
That's what professional grillers say.
I'm just a civilian.

22:06.033 --> 22:07.743
My mom says "burning the grill" too.

22:07.826 --> 22:09.286
Well, my mom doesn't.

22:10.287 --> 22:12.205
- For someone who knows meat--
- There!

22:12.706 --> 22:13.707
Get grilling.

22:13.790 --> 22:15.167
Well, I can't.

22:15.250 --> 22:17.544
You can't put meat on a lukewarm grill.

22:17.627 --> 22:19.838
Yes, that'll ruin the flavor.
You've got to wait.

22:22.799 --> 22:25.177
Shall we talk while the grill heats up?

22:26.136 --> 22:29.514
Gun-woo. Just speak naturally.

22:29.598 --> 22:31.391
Right. Are you and Mr. Choi related?

22:31.975 --> 22:34.603
What? That came out of left field.

22:34.686 --> 22:37.898
I was actually curious about that too.

22:39.816 --> 22:40.650
Well…

22:42.152 --> 22:43.487
Long story short.

22:45.989 --> 22:48.533
I was diagnosed with spinal cancer
when I was eight.

22:49.701 --> 22:52.037
I was cured by the time I was ten,

22:53.622 --> 22:56.083
but my dad passed away.

22:58.085 --> 23:00.128
So I was sent to an orphanage,

23:01.254 --> 23:03.173
but I hated it so much I ran away.

23:04.299 --> 23:06.093
I used to get so hungry,

23:07.052 --> 23:10.722
I ate leftover black bean sauce noodles
that people left on their doorsteps.

23:11.390 --> 23:13.725
I also worked at bars
with other runaway kids,

23:14.893 --> 23:16.186
but that was so hard.

23:18.230 --> 23:19.940
So I went back to the orphanage.

23:22.275 --> 23:25.570
I was dragged off to a different orphanage
when I was 17.

23:26.446 --> 23:28.365
Grandpa was the owner there.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.325
- Mr. Choi?
- Yes.

23:31.326 --> 23:33.829
He built an orphanage
to do something meaningful.

23:36.123 --> 23:38.166
He was really nice to me in particular.

23:38.875 --> 23:41.211
At first, I thought he might be a pervert,

23:42.838 --> 23:44.840
but I realized as time passed…

23:46.425 --> 23:48.093
he was just being himself.

23:48.176 --> 23:52.264
Grandpa let me learn everything I couldn't
because I didn't have the money.

23:52.347 --> 23:56.101
I learned Kendo
and how to ride a motorcycle.

24:01.982 --> 24:04.776
I can tell Mr. Choi is a nice person.

24:05.485 --> 24:06.778
Since middle school,

24:06.862 --> 24:09.489
I've worked part-time jobs with my mom
to pay off my dad's debt.

24:10.574 --> 24:14.411
When our debt grew to 100 million won,
I felt utterly helpless.

24:15.370 --> 24:18.206
I know how scary
a hundred million won can be.

24:18.707 --> 24:21.877
So when Mr. Choi gave me that money,
telling me to pay off my debts,

24:21.960 --> 24:23.211
I thought to myself

24:24.171 --> 24:26.923
that I need to protect this man
at all costs.

24:29.050 --> 24:32.762
Grandpa told me that in order
to judge someone's depth of character,

24:32.846 --> 24:34.431
I should open up my mind.

24:34.514 --> 24:38.143
People with depth of character will see
your earnestness and return it in kind,

24:38.935 --> 24:41.354
and those who lack depth
will use that against you.

24:42.606 --> 24:44.733
- That's true.
- You're a nice person, Gun-woo.

24:45.233 --> 24:49.154
Right. I'm good at being nice
and being diligent.

24:49.779 --> 24:51.656
- I think we can start grilling now.
- Sure.

25:01.082 --> 25:03.168
Talk about perfect timing.

25:03.251 --> 25:04.127
You're learning.

25:04.211 --> 25:06.338
I learned from the best, right?

25:06.963 --> 25:09.424
I suddenly feel left out.

25:10.967 --> 25:12.719
Never mind. Hurry up and flip it.

25:12.802 --> 25:13.720
I can't do that.

25:13.803 --> 25:15.180
Trust him. He's good at this.

25:15.847 --> 25:17.933
God, I can't get used to
this conversation.

25:18.016 --> 25:19.142
Okay, take your time.

25:21.853 --> 25:22.812
Smells amazing.

25:25.440 --> 25:27.442
- Let's clean out the buffet today.
- Sure.

25:28.026 --> 25:30.195
- When do you get the stitches out?
- Tomorrow.

25:30.278 --> 25:31.279
Does it hurt?

25:31.363 --> 25:32.572
Well, it's bearable.

25:33.865 --> 25:37.118
- I asked for mine hot.
- It's better cold in the winter.

25:37.202 --> 25:38.912
Jeez, seriously.

25:39.538 --> 25:40.705
- Hyeon-ju.
- Yes.

25:40.789 --> 25:44.167
Yang Jae-myeong knows our location.
Shouldn't we do something about it?

25:45.961 --> 25:47.963
I'll talk it over with Grandpa.

25:49.339 --> 25:51.716
- Ask quickly. We don't have time.
- Okay.

25:53.635 --> 25:54.511
Ms. Lee.

25:55.095 --> 25:57.055
The lobby is a hotel's first impression.

25:57.556 --> 26:00.809
I want our international guests
to see the most Korean, beautiful,

26:00.892 --> 26:02.352
and majestic lobby there is.

26:02.435 --> 26:05.397
The kind of thing
they've never experienced before.

26:05.480 --> 26:06.690
Yes, I understand.

26:06.773 --> 26:07.816
TEAM LEADER LEE SO-HYEON

26:07.899 --> 26:10.569
I look forward to hearing
your brilliant ideas

26:10.652 --> 26:11.653
at the meeting tomorrow.

26:12.153 --> 26:15.782
Our casino will be
on the top floor of that hotel.

26:15.865 --> 26:19.119
My goal is 100 billion won
in annual revenue.

26:19.202 --> 26:20.829
There are a lot of people

26:20.912 --> 26:24.207
itching for a fix now that
gambling in Macau's been blocked off.

26:24.791 --> 26:29.254
We'll book them a suite
every week to let them have fun.

26:30.338 --> 26:32.674
We'll secretly catch them
gambling on camera.

26:32.757 --> 26:35.468
Once we have enough cash,

26:36.136 --> 26:41.850
Jang-do will hand over the evidence
of illegal gambling to the police.

26:43.602 --> 26:46.104
When the hotel is ruined
and worth nothing,

26:47.063 --> 26:50.191
we'll swoop in
and take over the whole thing.

26:58.992 --> 27:01.161
Once Jang-do returns
with dirt on Director Hong,

27:01.244 --> 27:03.246
we need to be ready to spend 100 billion.

27:03.330 --> 27:06.082
We're currently
about 50 billion short, right?

27:06.166 --> 27:07.000
Yes, sir.

27:08.043 --> 27:10.545
It's time to collect on everything.

27:11.880 --> 27:14.382
Sell off anything that's of any value.

27:15.467 --> 27:16.885
Coming through!

27:24.309 --> 27:25.268
Yes, sir.

27:25.352 --> 27:27.854
That car you mentioned just came in.

27:27.937 --> 27:29.105
Okay.

27:30.440 --> 27:31.858
I'll be right back, sir.

27:43.745 --> 27:44.579
What's going on?

27:51.252 --> 27:52.170
CAR WASH EXIT
NO PARKING

27:53.380 --> 27:54.214
Hello!

27:56.216 --> 27:58.093
What's happening? Damn it.

28:00.845 --> 28:02.305
Look at this guy.

28:13.441 --> 28:15.527
- Keep them down.
- Damn it!

28:22.325 --> 28:24.452
That's gross, man. Damn it.

28:26.287 --> 28:27.497
What is this punk doing?

28:27.580 --> 28:29.332
Spare me.

28:29.416 --> 28:30.250
Grab him!

28:30.333 --> 28:32.711
You're fucking dead, you son of a bitch.

28:33.503 --> 28:35.046
Where are you going?

28:35.547 --> 28:37.257
Hey, strip him down.

28:38.675 --> 28:41.094
Hey, come here.

28:46.558 --> 28:48.518
Hello, sir. Right this way.

28:48.601 --> 28:50.311
- Is he in there right now?
- Yes.

28:50.395 --> 28:51.730
Thank you for your hard work.

28:54.107 --> 28:55.692
- You can count it.
- Thank you, sir.

28:56.192 --> 28:58.361
- You son of a bitch.
- Fuck.

28:58.445 --> 29:01.781
I'm sorry.
Please give me something to wear.

29:03.783 --> 29:05.702
You boys sure did a number on him.

29:05.785 --> 29:06.995
- Hello, sir!
- Hello, sir!

29:07.078 --> 29:09.998
It's too cold.
Can you give me some clothes?

29:10.707 --> 29:11.624
I'm sorry, sir.

29:16.504 --> 29:17.422
Hi there.

29:21.301 --> 29:22.218
You…

29:23.720 --> 29:25.430
It's you, isn't it? Fuck.

29:25.930 --> 29:27.390
Motherfucker.

29:28.558 --> 29:30.810
You were acting like hot shit.

29:32.228 --> 29:33.396
Prick.

29:34.105 --> 29:34.939
You know,

29:35.690 --> 29:38.610
you shouldn't have fucked around with him.

29:39.778 --> 29:41.529
Did you think he'd get scared

29:41.613 --> 29:43.865
and apologize to you or something

29:43.948 --> 29:46.618
just because your cousin's a cop?

29:54.918 --> 29:57.629
Let me teach you a valuable lesson.

29:58.838 --> 30:02.842
Untamed animals bite back if you hit them.

30:04.552 --> 30:08.097
It doesn't matter how much stronger
or weaker you are than them.

30:08.598 --> 30:10.308
They just bite back.

30:18.983 --> 30:20.276
Now then.

30:23.363 --> 30:24.197
Strip down.

30:24.280 --> 30:25.448
What?

30:25.532 --> 30:27.742
Take off your underwear.

30:27.826 --> 30:29.452
Okay, I get it now.

30:29.536 --> 30:31.496
Please let me off just this once.

30:31.579 --> 30:33.915
- Damn it.
- I'm sorry.

30:33.998 --> 30:35.416
I don't know what it's about…

30:35.500 --> 30:36.543
Hey, In-beom.

30:37.502 --> 30:39.170
Let me off the hook just this once.

30:43.299 --> 30:44.509
Let's wrap it up.

30:55.520 --> 30:56.688
Do you want to strip or not?

30:58.731 --> 31:00.108
Don't kill me.

31:00.900 --> 31:02.610
- Please let me live.
- Drink some more.

31:07.282 --> 31:08.741
Do you want to strip or not?

31:18.251 --> 31:20.128
I'll strip down!

31:20.712 --> 31:21.629
Right now.

31:26.843 --> 31:28.303
Good call.

31:28.887 --> 31:31.556
Director Hong, let's see you strip.

31:49.157 --> 31:50.491
I GOT SOMETHING BIG

31:50.575 --> 31:52.660
All right, that's enough.

32:02.086 --> 32:05.006
KICKBOXING

32:08.134 --> 32:09.260
Get it up. Come on.

32:28.988 --> 32:29.989
Yes.

32:30.073 --> 32:35.995
Mr. Choi, the Kim Myeong-gil we know
is indeed the CEO of Smile Capital.

32:36.663 --> 32:37.747
I see.

32:39.123 --> 32:41.542
I'm coming to pick you up.
I'll be there soon, sir.

32:42.043 --> 32:42.877
Okay.

33:04.565 --> 33:06.526
I'm sorry for the sudden decision.

33:09.487 --> 33:12.198
Recently, I've gone through
personal difficulties.

33:14.367 --> 33:18.204
It's been decided after much thought,
so I hope you'll understand.

33:19.539 --> 33:21.791
Our company will close
at the end of this month.

33:23.543 --> 33:25.044
I will be wiring you

33:25.795 --> 33:28.339
a year's wages and your severance pay.

33:32.427 --> 33:33.553
Thanks for everything.

33:34.512 --> 33:35.680
Sir, what about

33:37.390 --> 33:39.600
our money that's out there right now?

33:40.393 --> 33:41.769
I'll take care of it.

34:09.172 --> 34:11.049
Dad.

34:31.319 --> 34:33.821
- Yes.
- This is Oh In-muk in security, sir.

34:34.405 --> 34:36.449
I think robbers broke into your office.

34:37.325 --> 34:38.326
How many?

34:44.040 --> 34:45.166
I think there are two.

35:10.858 --> 35:11.692
Hey!

35:13.277 --> 35:14.946
You said ten minutes is enough.

35:15.446 --> 35:18.449
This model normally comes
with a six-digit combination.

35:18.533 --> 35:19.492
This one has eight.

35:19.575 --> 35:20.952
I think they modified it.

35:22.328 --> 35:24.580
- So what?
- I need more time.

35:25.331 --> 35:26.332
Hurry it up.

35:51.065 --> 35:51.899
I got it!

35:52.984 --> 35:54.735
Okay. Get out of the way.

36:03.494 --> 36:04.745
PRIVATE LOAN STANDARD AGREEMENT

36:04.829 --> 36:08.040
These promissory notes
are worth a billion won each.

36:27.268 --> 36:28.102
What happened?

36:28.186 --> 36:30.605
No one has come out.
I've stopped the elevator.

36:30.688 --> 36:31.856
I see.

36:32.523 --> 36:35.234
Well, shall I accompany you?

36:35.318 --> 36:37.987
No, that's fine. Thank you.

36:38.821 --> 36:41.073
Wait. Let me just borrow this.

36:41.157 --> 36:41.991
Sure.

37:17.860 --> 37:18.945
Who are you?

37:22.990 --> 37:24.116
How did you get in?

38:19.630 --> 38:20.673
Who sent you?

38:27.930 --> 38:29.181
Who sent you?

38:29.265 --> 38:30.099
Damn it.

38:30.933 --> 38:32.393
Who sent you?

38:35.896 --> 38:36.981
Who sent you?

38:38.149 --> 38:39.317
Who sent you?

39:00.629 --> 39:01.839
Fuck.

40:34.265 --> 40:35.474
Sir, are you okay?

40:35.558 --> 40:36.684
Kill that bastard!

41:25.691 --> 41:27.067
It's okay, Beom. Okay?

41:27.151 --> 41:29.153
- Snap out of it, Beom.
- Okay.

41:29.236 --> 41:30.488
- Yes?
- Yes, sir.

41:30.571 --> 41:31.906
Kang In-beom!

41:34.033 --> 41:35.159
We don't have time.

41:35.242 --> 41:38.204
Take all the money in the safe
and head down first.

41:43.042 --> 41:45.294
Pull yourself together.

42:17.243 --> 42:18.202
Sir!

42:19.453 --> 42:20.788
He's gone.

42:26.043 --> 42:27.461
- Go down first.
- Yes, sir.

42:49.233 --> 42:50.901
- Mr. Choi.
- Yes?

43:20.514 --> 43:22.182
Have you given it some thought?

43:26.478 --> 43:28.314
Come on. What's the issue here?

43:29.523 --> 43:31.191
Let's avoid Yang Jae-myeong.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.152
Why?

43:33.652 --> 43:35.613
They kill people.

43:35.696 --> 43:37.573
Let's also move the bookstore.

43:38.157 --> 43:39.199
Why?

43:39.283 --> 43:40.451
Hyeon-ju.

43:43.621 --> 43:44.788
Look at me.

43:48.584 --> 43:50.544
I am old and tired.

43:51.128 --> 43:53.339
There's no strength or courage left in me

43:54.256 --> 43:55.674
to fight them.

43:56.175 --> 43:58.802
I want to live out
my remaining days in peace,

43:59.470 --> 44:04.642
teaching you the things
I want to teach you

44:06.352 --> 44:09.188
and giving you the things
I want to leave to you.

44:10.898 --> 44:13.108
That is my only wish.

44:17.946 --> 44:19.281
Can you help me with that?

44:25.371 --> 44:26.205
Good.

44:27.998 --> 44:29.041
Thank you.

45:52.416 --> 45:54.251
The value of gold is bound to rise

45:54.793 --> 45:57.463
whenever people lose confidence
in fiat currency.

45:57.546 --> 46:01.175
That's why it's safest
to have your slush fund in gold.

46:01.967 --> 46:04.344
If you melt gold
and mix it with other gold,

46:04.428 --> 46:06.597
it practically launders itself.

46:07.973 --> 46:10.309
That's the first thing
I learned from Choi.

46:14.396 --> 46:16.899
Failing to get my hands
on his hidden gold…

46:19.526 --> 46:20.778
I still regret it.

46:21.403 --> 46:23.489
That old fuck.

46:24.323 --> 46:26.992
Why did he have to close the damn company?

47:20.045 --> 47:21.088
Beom.

47:21.171 --> 47:22.130
Yes, sir.

47:22.965 --> 47:24.007
Get in here.

47:35.435 --> 47:36.395
What do you think?

47:37.646 --> 47:38.605
It's amazing.

47:43.694 --> 47:45.279
Each bar is worth 500 million.

47:45.362 --> 47:47.531
If our business in Korea goes south,

47:48.740 --> 47:51.702
you and I will take this
and go to Vietnam.

47:52.911 --> 47:56.999
I planted someone
in the Vietnamese government.

47:57.958 --> 47:58.792
With this,

48:00.419 --> 48:03.005
we should be able to live like kings
for the rest of our days.

48:05.757 --> 48:06.717
Thank you, sir.

48:11.597 --> 48:13.473
You're my brother.

48:13.557 --> 48:16.143
I would do anything for you.

48:17.436 --> 48:18.270
Beom.

48:20.814 --> 48:23.901
You're all I've got.

48:25.485 --> 48:26.486
You know that, right?

48:33.619 --> 48:34.786
Come on.

48:36.455 --> 48:38.707
They have the best stir-fried pork
in the world.

48:38.790 --> 48:40.417
- It's that good?
- Yes.

48:50.177 --> 48:51.929
Auntie?

48:53.305 --> 48:55.766
Auntie.

48:56.808 --> 48:57.809
Yes, it's Woo-jin.

48:58.310 --> 49:01.271
Oh God, Woo-jin.

49:02.064 --> 49:03.106
What happened?

49:04.316 --> 49:06.735
I took out a private loan.

49:07.861 --> 49:09.321
They told me to pay them back.

49:09.404 --> 49:12.449
I told them I didn't have money
because my business isn't doing well.

49:13.533 --> 49:14.952
They smashed everything.

49:15.035 --> 49:16.995
God, I'm scared.

49:19.247 --> 49:20.540
What should I do?

49:26.338 --> 49:29.007
She can't run her business
because you wrecked the place.

49:29.091 --> 49:31.468
How do you expect her
to pay back your interest now?

49:31.551 --> 49:33.053
She wasn't paying back.

49:33.136 --> 49:35.764
I'm saying go easy.
Times are tough for everyone.

49:35.847 --> 49:38.058
Then how am I supposed to make a living?

49:38.141 --> 49:40.102
Why don't you pay for her?

49:40.811 --> 49:43.563
You know I don't have the money for that.

49:43.647 --> 49:45.190
Then just shut your mouth.

49:45.273 --> 49:48.485
Mind your own business. Got it?

49:49.027 --> 49:49.945
Fine.

49:59.329 --> 50:00.205
It's Im.

50:01.623 --> 50:03.208
He's a guy I used to work with.

50:03.291 --> 50:06.086
He got conned recently
by someone he lent 500 million won to.

50:06.169 --> 50:08.005
- Is it Yang Jae-myeong?
- I don't know.

50:08.088 --> 50:09.798
I didn't ask for the details.

50:10.298 --> 50:13.093
But it was a homeless person's ID
and a mule account.

50:13.593 --> 50:14.511
Identical MO.

50:15.095 --> 50:16.054
It is him.

50:17.556 --> 50:18.390
We should catch him.

50:20.517 --> 50:22.519
I'm a victim too. I just can't do nothing.

50:23.395 --> 50:25.063
Grandpa told us to lie low.

50:25.814 --> 50:27.190
They're dangerous people.

50:27.274 --> 50:29.526
I think it's wrong to do nothing.

50:30.152 --> 50:31.528
What if I call him back

50:31.611 --> 50:33.613
and tell him about Yang
so he can catch him?

50:34.823 --> 50:36.908
If the goal is to catch him,
we should do it.

50:37.409 --> 50:38.577
We might make money.

50:38.660 --> 50:42.289
If we make money from this,
can I use it to help Auntie?

50:42.372 --> 50:45.375
We'll split it evenly.
Feel free to use it however you see fit.

50:46.626 --> 50:49.254
- All right.
- Then I want to help her too.

50:53.091 --> 50:53.925
Come over here.

50:57.763 --> 50:58.638
Come on over.

50:58.722 --> 50:59.639
Damn it.

51:02.642 --> 51:03.560
Thank you.

51:18.033 --> 51:18.867
All in.

51:32.005 --> 51:34.424
Sir, you should take a look at this.

51:37.094 --> 51:38.386
That car.

51:39.513 --> 51:42.015
They turned off the engine,
but no one's getting out.

51:44.810 --> 51:46.269
- Get ready.
- Yes, sir.

51:47.437 --> 51:48.855
Hey, check your phone.

51:48.939 --> 51:49.773
Yes, sir.

51:56.822 --> 51:58.448
Sir, they're here.

51:59.658 --> 52:02.035
Do exactly as I say in two hours.

52:26.101 --> 52:27.102
They're here.

52:35.777 --> 52:36.903
Let's go.

52:42.534 --> 52:44.578
You're gonna die today, fuckers.

53:49.851 --> 53:50.977
Yes, sir.

53:52.187 --> 53:53.313
You can come down now.

54:03.448 --> 54:04.532
Come on out!

54:05.492 --> 54:08.536
I know you're there, so hurry up
and show yourselves, fuckers!

54:09.037 --> 54:12.123
Come out, you son of a bitch!
Are you playing hide-and-seek?

54:12.624 --> 54:13.500
Motherfuckers.

54:27.764 --> 54:30.225
Please pick up…

54:30.308 --> 54:32.185
HYEON-JU

